From e665ee58031e656eb21b79eca34bf40ec2d5c682 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 13:25:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 01/22] Fix liked-songs order, artwork resolution, and
 BetterLyrics; port Metrolist's sync engine

Sync engine (app/utils/SyncUtils.kt, rewritten)
Adopts Metrolist's architecture while keeping OuterTune's feature set:
a single-consumer Channel queue with per-category coalescing keys, one
non-reentrant Mutex serialising every sync body, retry with exponential
backoff, and a structured SyncState/SyncStatus per category. The old
boolean StateFlows are kept as derived values so existing UI compiles
and behaves unchanged. SyncContent gating, SyncConflictResolution,
per-category cooldown keys and the isLocal exclusions are all preserved.

Bugs fixed along the way:
- The "already syncing" guard was inverted, so a second request would
  proceed precisely when one was already running.
- SYNC_CD was a millisecond value (60000 * 30) compared against a delta
  measured in seconds, and the comparison was inverted: the cooldown
  rejected syncs that were due and allowed ones that weren't. Replaced
  with SYNC_COOLDOWN in seconds; SYNC_CD is deprecated.
- runBlocking inside suspend functions blocked sync threads; replaced
  with structured concurrency.
- Last*SyncKey timestamps were written in a finally block even when the
  sync had bailed out or failed, suppressing retries for a full cooldown
  window. They are now written only on success.
- syncPlaylist would clear a local playlist when the remote page came
  back empty.

Liked-songs ordering
YouTube exposes no per-song like timestamp; position in the LM playlist
is the only ordering signal. The previous code reversed the page, stamped
likedDate with LocalDateTime.now() per song, and skipped songs already
liked locally, so their liked date stayed frozen at whenever they were
first seen and local order drifted permanently out of step with YouTube.
Now likedDate is derived from the song's index in the unreversed remote
list and re-stamped every sync, so sorting the Liked playlist by liked
date reproduces YouTube's order exactly.

Album artwork resolution (+ toggle)
getThumbnailModel and ItemThumbnail passed remote URLs to Coil verbatim,
so the ~60-226px thumbnails YouTube returns in browse and library
responses were upscaled to fill the view. Artwork is now requested at the
size it will actually be drawn, via a new remoteArtwork() helper applied
in ItemThumbnail, the player cover, and AlbumScreen. Controlled by a new
"High resolution artwork" switch in Appearance settings (default on).

BetterLyrics
The provider was off by default, sent no User-Agent (which the API
rejects) and had no timeout. More importantly OuterTune's strict TTML2
parser requires a <head> element right after <tt>, which many
BetterLyrics responses omit, so lyrics became an "Unable to parse
lyrics" placeholder and were classified UNPARSEABLE on the fetch path
and discarded. Adds a lenient TTML reader ported from Metrolist that
emits plain line-by-line LRC as a fallback, keeping the strict parser
(and its word-level karaoke timing) as the primary path.

Player lyrics toggle
Removes the dedicated lyrics button from the player controls. Lyrics are
toggled by tapping the cover or via the overflow menu, as in older
OuterTune.

