From 148bf5b705afa6dfc04b89fabb3aa97cd4a286ae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 06:58:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/22] Add Discord rich presence

Ported from reocat/OuterTune rather than Metrolist: it is already
OuterTune-shaped, so it drops into the same Song entity and MusicService
rather than needing a translation layer, and it is roughly half the code.

The presence carries a real progress bar. startTime is anchored to
(now - playback position) and endTime to (now + remaining), which is the
same mechanism Spotify's own integration uses, and it is re-sent whenever
the song changes or playback starts, so seeking and pausing re-anchor the
bar instead of letting it drift. Album art is the large image, artist art
the small one, with buttons linking to the track and the project.

The kizzy module is vendored as-is (its own license header applies). The
two settings screens were rebuilt with OuterTune's own PreferenceEntry /
SwitchPreference / PreferenceGroupTitle components instead of copying the
donor's, so they match the rest of settings; the elaborate presence
preview from the donor screen was left out.

Note on how this authenticates: Kizzy drives the Discord gateway with the
user's own account token, obtained by signing in through a WebView. That
is what Discord's terms call a self-bot. The upstream string already warns
about it and that warning is shown on the settings screen.

