From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 07:47:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/22] Add a Liquid player background

A slow breathing wash of colour taken from the current album art, offered
alongside Follow theme / Gradient / Blur in Appearance settings. Three
radial gradients drift on out-of-phase sine curves so the loop never
visibly repeats, with a gentle overall pulse.

Not driven by the audio signal, on purpose. Reading PCM would mean putting
an AudioProcessor into the sink chain, which is the code path that produces
sound and a poor place for a change that cannot be tested here. Amplitude
data is also spiky enough that anything calm enough to sit behind a player
ends up smoothed past the point where the audio still shows through.

Cost is a few radial gradients per frame, and the animation values are read
inside drawBehind so a frame redraws without recomposing. The clock stops
entirely while playback is paused or battery saver is on; a collapsed
player sheet already drops it from composition. It reuses the palette
extraction that Gradient already performs, so it adds no image work.

