release build, so a gateway that never connected looked exactly like a
presence that was never sent. Three changes:

The socket now records what happened to it in words - connecting,
connected, the close code, or the exception - and calls out 4004
specifically, since that means Discord rejected the token.

sendActivity no longer loops forever waiting to identify. It waits 15
seconds and gives up, so a connection that cannot succeed surfaces instead
of leaving the caller suspended for the life of the process.

Settings gains a "Test connection" row that opens a gateway connection on
demand and reports the outcome, so the failure can be identified without a
logcat.

