From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 11:10:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] Stop reporting the previous track's position to Discord

player.currentPosition can still refer to the outgoing item while a track
transition settles, so the presence was published with an elapsed time
taken from the previous song - 2:22 already gone against the new track's
shorter length, which Discord renders as a broken bar. Pressing previous
appeared to fix it only because rewinding resets the position to zero,
which is also why changing songs never did.

The position is now only trusted when player.currentMediaItem agrees on
which song it is; otherwise the track is treated as starting from zero,
which is what a fresh transition means anyway. Applied at all three places
that publish a presence.

Presence writes are also serialised now, with superseded ones dropped.
setActivity resolves both artwork URLs over the network before sending, so
the track-change collector and the play/pause hook can overlap, and the
older write could land last and leave the card describing the previous
song. The collector uses collectLatest for the same reason.

