Subject: [PATCH 22/22] Ask Discord's module registry for the token

The WebView login read localStorage, which Discord's client no longer
reliably populates - that is why the login page just sat there. Push a
webpack chunk instead and ask the module that owns the token for it
directly, which does not depend on where the client happens to keep the
value. localStorage and the iframe read stay on as fallbacks.

Method contributed by @notK50BML, who found it works on both the web and
desktop clients.

Tokens are also normalised now, at all three entry points. localStorage
holds the value JSON-encoded, so it arrives wrapped in quote characters,
and a token copied out of a console picks them up the same way. Those
quotes reach the gateway as part of the token and come back as a bare
close code 4004 with nothing to explain it.
